{
  "name": "graal",
  "description": "GraalVM is a high-performance polyglot virtual machine and compiler infrastructure supporting both just-in-time (JIT) and ahead-of-time (AOT) execution. It utilizes the Truffle framework to implement language runtimes for JVM-based, LLVM-based, and dynamic languages while providing SubstrateVM for compiling applications into standalone native binaries. The architecture incorporates advanced optimization techniques such as speculative compilation, partial evaluation, and aggressive escape analysis to achieve peak performance across heterogeneous workloads.",
